(doc
  (title "Interoperability Testing Requirements")
  (source-format markdown)
  (converted "2026-07-19")
  (para "**Status:** MANDATORY **Priority:** CRITICAL **Skip Policy:** CANNOT BE SKIPPED")
  (section
    (heading "Overview")
    (para "This specification defines the **mandatory interoperability testing requirements** for the YX protocol. Wire format compatibility or in-memory byte comparison is **NOT sufficient**. All language implementations **MUST** demonstrate actual UDP network communication with verified packet exchange."))
  (section
    (heading "Core Principle")
    (para "**Interoperability MUST be proven with running code, not assumptions.**")
    (item "❌ **NOT SUFFICIENT:** \"The packets are byte-identical in memory\"")
    (item "❌ **NOT SUFFICIENT:** \"The wire format matches the spec\"")
    (item "❌ **NOT SUFFICIENT:** \"Canonical test vectors pass\"")
    (item "✅ **REQUIRED:** Actual UDP packets sent over network and received successfully"))
  (section
    (heading "Mandatory Test Matrix")
    (para "Every language implementation MUST be tested in all 4 combinations:")
    (table
      (row "Test ID" "Sender" "Receiver" "Status" "Required")
      (row "IT-01" "Python" "Python" "-" "✅ MANDATORY")
      (row "IT-02" "Python" "Swift" "-" "✅ MANDATORY")
      (row "IT-03" "Swift" "Python" "-" "✅ MANDATORY")
      (row "IT-04" "Swift" "Swift" "-" "✅ MANDATORY"))
    (para "**For N language implementations, N² tests are required.**")
    (para "Example with 4 languages (Python, Swift, Rust, Go):")
    (item "4 × 4 = **16 mandatory interop tests**"))
  (section
    (heading "Test Requirements")
    (subsection
      (heading "1. Network Communication Required")
      (para "All tests MUST:")
      (item "✅ Use real UDP sockets (not mocks, not in-memory)")
      (item "✅ Bind to actual network ports")
      (item "✅ Send packets over localhost (127.0.0.1)")
      (item "✅ Use OS network stack (real UDP/IP)")
      (item "❌ NOT use in-memory queues or mocks"))
    (subsection
      (heading "2. Packet Verification Required")
      (para "All tests MUST verify:")
      (item "✅ Packet sent successfully")
      (item "✅ Packet received within timeout (e.g., 5 seconds)")
      (item "✅ HMAC validates correctly")
      (item "✅ GUID matches expected value")
      (item "✅ Payload matches expected value")
      (item "✅ Packet length is correct"))
    (subsection
      (heading "3. Test Scenarios Required")
      (para "Each test MUST cover:")
      (item "1. **Simple payload** - ASCII text (e.g., \"Hello from {language}!\")")
      (item "2. **Empty payload** - Zero-byte payload")
      (item "3. **Large payload** - At least 5KB payload")
      (item "4. **Multiple packets** - Send/receive at least 10 packets sequentially")
      (item "5. **Invalid key rejection** - Receiver MUST reject packet with wrong key"))
    (subsection
      (heading "4. Test Execution Required")
      (para "All tests MUST:")
      (item "✅ Run in under 30 seconds (total)")
      (item "✅ Pass 100% of the time (no flaky tests)")
      (item "✅ Be runnable with single command")
      (item "✅ Report clear pass/fail status")
      (item "✅ Log actual bytes sent/received for debugging")))
  (section
    (heading "Implementation Requirements")
    (subsection
      (heading "API Compatibility")
      (para "To enable interop testing, all implementations MUST provide:")
      (item "1. **Sender Interface**")
      (item "Function/method to send packet to arbitrary host:port")
      (item "Parameters: GUID, payload, key, destination host, destination port")
      (item "Return: Success/failure indication")
      (item "2. **Receiver Interface**")
      (item "Function/method to receive packet with timeout")
      (item "Parameters: Key, port to bind, timeout duration")
      (item "Return: Received packet (GUID, payload) or timeout error")
      (item "3. **Unified Key Format**")
      (item "All implementations MUST accept keys as raw bytes OR")
      (item "Provide conversion utilities between language-specific types"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Executable Requirements")
      (para "Each implementation MUST provide:")
      (item "1. **Standalone Sender**")
      (item "Executable: `{language}-sender`")
      (item "Usage: `{language}-sender <payload> <host> <port>`")
      (item "Outputs: \"SENT: {payload}\" on success")
      (item "Exit code: 0 on success, non-zero on failure")
      (item "2. **Standalone Receiver**")
      (item "Executable: `{language}-receiver`")
      (item "Usage: `{language}-receiver <port>`")
      (item "Outputs: \"RECEIVED: {payload}\" on success")
      (item "Exit code: 0 on success, non-zero on failure")
      (item "3. **Shared Configuration**")
      (item "Use fixed test key: 32 bytes of 0x00 for interop tests")
      (item "Use fixed test GUID: 6 bytes of 0x01 for interop tests")
      (item "Default timeout: 5 seconds")))
  (section
    (heading "Test Harness Requirements")
    (subsection
      (heading "Orchestration")
      (para "The test harness MUST:")
      (item "Start receiver process in background")
      (item "Wait for receiver to bind (e.g., 1 second)")
      (item "Start sender process")
      (item "Wait for completion (timeout: 5 seconds)")
      (item "Verify both processes succeeded")
      (item "Clean up all processes"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Error Reporting")
      (para "The test harness MUST report:")
      (item "Which test combination failed (e.g., \"Python → Swift FAILED\")")
      (item "What went wrong (e.g., \"Receiver timeout\", \"HMAC validation failed\")")
      (item "Actual bytes sent vs received (for debugging)")
      (item "Network errors (e.g., \"Port already in use\")"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Test Isolation")
      (para "Each test MUST:")
      (item "Use unique port number (avoid conflicts)")
      (item "Clean up processes after test")
      (item "Not depend on previous test state")
      (item "Be runnable in any order")))
  (section
    (heading "Success Criteria")
    (para "Interoperability testing is **COMPLETE** when:")
    (para "✅ All N² test combinations pass (transport layer) ✅ All N² protocol test combinations pass (text + binary) ✅ All test scenarios pass for each combination ✅ Tests run reliably (no flaky failures) ✅ Single command runs all tests ✅ Clear pass/fail reporting")
    (para "**Completion Definition:**")
    (code "Transport tests = N² × 5 scenarios
Text protocol tests = N² × 3 scenarios
Binary protocol tests = N² × 4 scenarios
Total tests = N² × 12 scenarios
Success = 100% pass rate")
    (para "For Python + Swift (N=2):")
    (code "Transport: 2² × 5 = 20 tests
Text Protocol: 2² × 3 = 12 tests
Binary Protocol: 2² × 4 = 16 tests
Total tests = 52 tests
Success = 52/52 passing"))
  (section
    (heading "Failure Handling")
    (para "If ANY interop test fails:")
    (item "1. ❌ Implementation is NOT considered complete")
    (item "2. ❌ Cannot promote to canonical/")
    (item "3. ❌ Cannot claim \"production ready\"")
    (item "4. ❌ Cannot claim \"interoperable\"")
    (para "**No exceptions. No workarounds. Must fix and pass.**"))
  (section
    (heading "Anti-Patterns (DO NOT DO THIS)")
    (subsection
      (heading "❌ Anti-Pattern 1: Mock Network")
      (code "# WRONG - This does not prove UDP interop
def test_interop():
    packet = sender.build_packet()
    result = receiver.parse_packet(packet)  # In-memory, no network
    assert result == expected"))
    (subsection
      (heading "❌ Anti-Pattern 2: Assume from Wire Format")
      (code "# WRONG - Byte-identical packets don't prove UDP works
def test_interop():
    python_packet = python_sender.build()
    swift_packet = swift_sender.build()
    assert python_packet == swift_packet  # Only proves format, not network"))
    (subsection
      (heading "❌ Anti-Pattern 3: Skip Combinations")
      (code "# WRONG - Must test ALL combinations
def test_interop():
    test_python_to_python()  # Only 1 of 4 required tests
    # Skipping Python→Swift, Swift→Python, Swift→Swift"))
    (subsection
      (heading "✅ Correct Pattern: Real Network Communication")
      (code "# CORRECT - Actual UDP communication
def test_interop():
    receiver = start_receiver(port=7777)
    time.sleep(1)  # Wait for bind
    sender.send_udp(payload=\"test\", host=\"127.0.0.1\", port=7777)
    received = receiver.wait_for_packet(timeout=5)
    assert received.payload == b\"test\"")))
  (section
    (heading "Standalone Test Suite Requirement ⚠️ MANDATORY")
    (subsection
      (heading "Comprehensive Test Runner")
      (para "A **standalone, self-contained test suite** MUST be provided that:")
      (item "1. ✅ Runs with a single command (no setup, no configuration)")
      (item "2. ✅ Tests ALL N² language combinations")
      (item "3. ✅ Tests ALL 5 scenarios per combination")
      (item "4. ✅ Tests BOTH Protocol 0 (Text) and Protocol 1 (Binary)")
      (item "5. ✅ Reports clear pass/fail for each test")
      (item "6. ✅ Reports overall summary")
      (item "7. ✅ Exits with code 0 on success, non-zero on any failure")
      (item "8. ✅ Can be run in CI/CD pipelines")
      (item "9. ✅ Handles timeouts and cleanup automatically")
      (item "10. ✅ Logs detailed output for debugging failures")
      (para "**Single Command Requirement:**")
      (code "./tests/interop/run_all_interop_tests.sh")
      (para "**No Setup Required:**")
      (item "Must not require manual process starting")
      (item "Must not require configuration file editing")
      (item "Must not require environment variables (except optional overrides)")
      (item "Must handle port allocation automatically")
      (item "Must clean up processes on exit (success or failure)")
      (para "**Output Requirement:**")
      (item "Must show progress in real-time")
      (item "Must report each test result immediately")
      (item "Must provide summary at end")
      (item "Must be parseable by CI/CD tools")))
  (section
    (heading "Test Location")
    (para "All interoperability tests MUST be located in:")
    (code "tests/interop/
├── transport/                      # UDP transport layer tests
│   ├── test_python_to_python.py
│   ├── test_python_to_swift.py
│   ├── test_swift_to_python.py
│   └── test_swift_to_swift.py
├── protocol/                       # Protocol layer tests (NEW)
│   ├── test_text_protocol.py      # Protocol 0 interop
│   └── test_binary_protocol.py    # Protocol 1 interop
├── run_all_interop_tests.sh       # Master test runner
└── README.md                       # Test documentation")
    (para "Single command to run all tests:")
    (code "./tests/interop/run_all_interop_tests.sh")
    (para "Expected output:")
    (code "Running YX Protocol Interoperability Tests...

========================================
PART 1: TRANSPORT LAYER TESTS (UDP + HMAC)
========================================

Test 1/4: Python → Python
  ✅ Simple payload: PASS
  ✅ Empty payload: PASS
  ✅ Large payload: PASS
  ✅ Multiple packets: PASS
  ✅ Invalid key rejection: PASS

Test 2/4: Python → Swift
  ✅ Simple payload: PASS
  ✅ Empty payload: PASS
  ✅ Large payload: PASS
  ✅ Multiple packets: PASS
  ✅ Invalid key rejection: PASS

Test 3/4: Swift → Python
  ✅ Simple payload: PASS
  ✅ Empty payload: PASS
  ✅ Large payload: PASS
  ✅ Multiple packets: PASS
  ✅ Invalid key rejection: PASS

Test 4/4: Swift → Swift
  ✅ Simple payload: PASS
  ✅ Empty payload: PASS
  ✅ Large payload: PASS
  ✅ Multiple packets: PASS
  ✅ Invalid key rejection: PASS

Transport Layer: 20/20 tests passed

========================================
PART 2: PROTOCOL LAYER TESTS
========================================

Protocol 0 (Text Protocol) Tests:

Test 1/4: Python → Python (Text)
  ✅ JSON message: PASS
  ✅ Large JSON (>5KB): PASS
  ✅ Invalid JSON rejection: PASS

Test 2/4: Python → Swift (Text)
  ✅ JSON message: PASS
  ✅ Large JSON (>5KB): PASS
  ✅ Invalid JSON rejection: PASS

Test 3/4: Swift → Python (Text)
  ✅ JSON message: PASS
  ✅ Large JSON (>5KB): PASS
  ✅ Invalid JSON rejection: PASS

Test 4/4: Swift → Swift (Text)
  ✅ JSON message: PASS
  ✅ Large JSON (>5KB): PASS
  ✅ Invalid JSON rejection: PASS

Text Protocol: 12/12 tests passed

Protocol 1 (Binary Protocol) Tests:

Test 1/4: Python → Python (Binary)
  ✅ Binary message: PASS
  ✅ Compressed message: PASS
  ✅ Encrypted message: PASS
  ✅ Compressed + encrypted: PASS

Test 2/4: Python → Swift (Binary)
  ✅ Binary message: PASS
  ✅ Compressed message: PASS
  ✅ Encrypted message: PASS
  ✅ Compressed + encrypted: PASS

Test 3/4: Swift → Python (Binary)
  ✅ Binary message: PASS
  ✅ Compressed message: PASS
  ✅ Encrypted message: PASS
  ✅ Compressed + encrypted: PASS

Test 4/4: Swift → Swift (Binary)
  ✅ Binary message: PASS
  ✅ Compressed message: PASS
  ✅ Encrypted message: PASS
  ✅ Compressed + encrypted: PASS

Binary Protocol: 16/16 tests passed

========================================
SUMMARY
========================================
Transport Layer:  20/20 passed ✅
Text Protocol:    12/12 passed ✅
Binary Protocol:  16/16 passed ✅
----------------------------------------
Total:            52/52 passed ✅
========================================
✅ ALL INTEROPERABILITY TESTS PASSED
Exit code: 0"))
  (section
    (heading "Protocol Layer Testing Requirements ⚠️ MANDATORY")
    (para "In addition to transport layer tests (UDP + HMAC), ALL implementations MUST test protocol-level interoperability.")
    (subsection
      (heading "Protocol 0: Text Protocol Tests")
      (para "**Purpose:** Verify JSON message exchange works across implementations")
      (para "**Required Tests (per language combination):**")
      (item "1. **Simple JSON message** - Send/receive basic JSON object")
      (item "2. **Large JSON message** - Send/receive JSON ≥5KB")
      (item "3. **Invalid JSON rejection** - Receiver MUST reject malformed JSON")
      (para "**Verification:**")
      (item "JSON parses correctly in receiver")
      (item "All fields preserved (no data loss)")
      (item "Types preserved (strings, numbers, booleans, nulls, arrays, objects)")
      (para "**Example Test:**")
      (code "def test_text_protocol_python_to_swift():
    swift_receiver = start_swift_text_receiver(port=7777)
    message = {\"method\": \"test\", \"params\": {\"value\": 42}}
    python_sender.send_text(message, host=\"127.0.0.1\", port=7777)
    received = swift_receiver.wait_for_message(timeout=5)
    assert received[\"method\"] == \"test\"
    assert received[\"params\"][\"value\"] == 42"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Protocol 1: Binary Protocol Tests")
      (para "**Purpose:** Verify binary message exchange with compression/encryption works")
      (para "**Required Tests (per language combination):**")
      (item "1. **Binary message** - Send/receive raw binary data")
      (item "2. **Compressed message** - Send/receive ZLIB-compressed data")
      (item "3. **Encrypted message** - Send/receive AES-256-GCM encrypted data")
      (item "4. **Compressed + encrypted** - Send/receive data with both features")
      (item "5. **Compressed + encrypted MULTI-CHUNK** - the same, with a payload that SPANS SEVERAL PACKETS **after compression**")
      (para "**Verification:**")
      (item "Binary data preserved exactly (byte-identical)")
      (item "Compression/decompression works correctly")
      (item "Encryption/decryption works correctly")
      (item "Combined compression + encryption works correctly")
      (item "Chunking and reassembly work on the COMBINED path, and the packet count is ASSERTED (not merely printed)")
      (para "**Why scenario 5 is separate and mandatory (added 2026-08-02, from a real gap):**")
      (para "sdts ran scenario 4 with `\"COMPRESSED_ENCRYPTED_PAYLOAD\" x100` — 2,969 bytes of pure repetition. zlib crushed it to 241 bytes, a 12x shrink, so it fitted in ONE packet. The suite reported 4/4 for months and had NEVER exercised chunking on the most complex path in the protocol: compress -> encrypt -> CHUNK -> reassemble -> decrypt -> decompress. An ordering bug there was invisible.")
      (para "A payload big enough to chunk BEFORE compression is not sufficient — compression happens first, so the requirement is on the COMPRESSED size. Two payload shapes are required because they prove different things:")
      (item "**Incompressible** (e.g. a hash chain, hex-encoded): chunking must happen even when compression cannot help. The packet count has an information-theoretic FLOOR that no better compressor can defeat.")
      (item "**Highly compressible but large** (e.g. indexed repeating blocks): still several packets AFTER compression, which proves the ORDERING. Note that PURE repetition compresses ~400x and will collapse to one packet — index the blocks.")
      (para "**The count MUST be asserted, and a MISSING count MUST fail.** The failure mode here was silent adequacy: a green test that had quietly stopped testing what it claimed. An assertion that can be absent is an assertion that can rot.")
      (para "**Example Test:**")
      (code "def test_binary_protocol_swift_to_python():
    python_receiver = start_python_binary_receiver(port=7778)
    data = b'\\x01\\x02\\x03\\x04' * 1000  # 4KB binary data
    swift_sender.send_binary(data, compressed=True, encrypted=True,
                            host=\"127.0.0.1\", port=7778)
    received = python_receiver.wait_for_message(timeout=5)
    assert received == data  # Must be byte-identical"))
    (subsection
      (heading "Test Count Calculation")
      (para "For N language implementations:")
      (para "**Transport Layer:**")
      (item "N² combinations × 5 scenarios = N² × 5 tests")
      (para "**Text Protocol (Protocol 0):**")
      (item "N² combinations × 3 scenarios = N² × 3 tests")
      (para "**Binary Protocol (Protocol 1):**")
      (item "N² combinations × 5 scenarios = N² × 5 tests")
      (para "**Total:**")
      (item "N² × (5 + 3 + 5) = N² × 13 tests")
      (para "**For Python + Swift (N=2):**")
      (item "Transport: 4 × 5 = 20 tests")
      (item "Text Protocol: 4 × 3 = 12 tests")
      (item "Binary Protocol: 4 × 5 = 20 tests")
      (item "**Total: 52 tests**")
      (para "**All 52 tests MUST pass for system to be considered complete.**")))
  (section
    (heading "Build System Integration")
    (subsection
      (heading "YBS Step Requirements")
      (para "Each language implementation MUST include an interop testing step:")
      (para "**Python:**")
      (item "Step 11 (after Step 10): Run full interop test suite")
      (para "**Swift:**")
      (item "Step 11 (after Step 10): Run full interop test suite")
      (para "**Step 11 Title:** \"Cross-Language Interoperability Validation\"")
      (para "**Step 11 Success Criteria:**")
      (item "All N² × 13 tests pass (transport + text + binary protocols)")
      (item "For Python + Swift: 52/52 tests pass")
      (item "Clear reporting of which combinations tested")
      (item "All 3 test layers pass (transport, text protocol, binary protocol)")
      (item "No skipped tests")
      (item "Exit code 0 on success")
      (para "**Step 11 Cannot Be Skipped:**")
      (item "Build is NOT complete without passing interop tests")
      (item "Cannot promote to canonical/ without passing interop tests")
      (item "Step 11 is as mandatory as Step 1")))
  (section
    (heading "Rationale")
    (para "**Why is this so strict?**")
    (item "1. **Wire format compatibility ≠ Network compatibility**")
    (item "Byte-identical packets can still fail over UDP due to:")
    (item "Socket configuration issues")
    (item "Endianness problems")
    (item "Buffer size mismatches")
    (item "Timeout handling bugs")
    (item "2. **In-memory tests miss real-world issues**")
    (item "Port conflicts")
    (item "Network permissions")
    (item "OS-specific socket behavior")
    (item "Packet loss handling")
    (item "3. **Cross-language bugs are subtle**")
    (item "Type conversions (bytes vs SymmetricKey)")
    (item "API mismatches (parameter names)")
    (item "Error handling differences")
    (item "4. **Production deployments require certainty**")
    (item "Cannot assume compatibility")
    (item "Must prove with running code")
    (item "No surprises in production")
    (para "**This specification ensures YX protocol implementations are truly interoperable, not just theoretically compatible.**"))
  (section
    (heading "Version History")
    (item "**1.0.0** (2026-01-18): Initial specification")))
